understand 20% or 30% of the words.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:14.967
However, if you're starting from scratch, 
I doubt you'll understand anything.

00:15:14.967 --> 00:15:18.167
Or one or two that you heard 
at your best at some point.

00:15:18.167 --> 00:15:23.200
How does Steve Kaufmann start 
learning a language from scratch?

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:25.867
Because I don't think you start out
 understanding the 20% or the 30%,

00:15:25.867 --> 00:15:27.500
that's cheating.
You then understand the language.

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:29.800
How does that work?

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:35.000
Steve: I started out by listening 
to short stories.

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:39.167
I won't understand anything, 
but it will make sense to me.

00:15:39.167 --> 00:15:44.167
Then I'll read a phrase at a time,

00:15:44.167 --> 00:15:48.867
look up words, read it again, 
and listen to it again.

00:15:48.867 --> 00:15:52.200
And finally, I'm going to hear
 the three-minute mini-story.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:55.767
I won't understand much of it, 
so I'll read it again.

00:15:55.767 --> 00:16:00.167
And eventually after that, I'll be bored,

00:16:00.167 --> 00:16:05.400
so I'll put myself in the position 
to study the next short story.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.467
And I won't understand much.
282
00:16:07,467 --&gt; 00:16:10,567
But eventually I'll have heard it 20 times.

00:16:10.567 --> 00:16:14.233
And after 20 times of hearing, 
five times of reading,

00:16:14.233 --> 00:16:19.733
and saving phrases and words, 
the noise will gradually 

00:16:19.733 --> 00:16:21.767
begin to make sense.

00:16:21.767 --> 00:16:27.200
This process, which I've used numerous times,
 is effective.

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:30.833
Since there is so much repetition 
in the short stories,

00:16:30.833 --> 00:16:35.767
this works.

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:47.100
Numerous beginner's books fall short 
of having enough repetitions.

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:54.233
When we first start, we'll have 
to run into those words a lot.

00:16:54.233 --> 00:16:55.567
a lot, a lot of times.

00:16:55.567 --> 00:17:00.833
The same words, the same vocabulary, 
and the same story

00:17:00.833 --> 00:17:04.833
all appear four or five times in one story.

00:17:04.833 --> 00:17:08.000
And so, after three months,

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:14.067
I can gradually start looking for more interesting 
YouTube content or whatever.

00:17:16.567 --> 00:17:17.800
Alberto: Contenido real, ¿no?

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.367
Steve: Yes, real. 

00:17:19.367 --> 00:17:24.300
However, we can continue talking for hours on end

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:26.367
and will continue on your channel.

00:17:26.367 --> 00:17:27.700
Alberto: Exactly. 

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:32.100
I invite you to watch the following video
 on my channel.

